\title{tulpaRatio: Bayesian Hierarchical Models for Ratios, Rates, and Proportions}
\description{
An opinionated framework for Bayesian hierarchical modelling of ratios, rates, and proportions. Ratios are treated as derived quantities, with all inference performed on the latent processes generating the numerator and denominator. Supports shared random effects, latent factors for unmeasured confounders, spatial structure ('CAR'/'BYM2'/'GP'), spatiotemporal interaction (Knorr-Held Type I-IV), zero-inflation variants, and full uncertainty propagation to ratio posteriors. Provides multiple inference backends including custom 'HMC'/'NUTS' (default), 'Laplace' approximation, and 'Polya-Gamma' Gibbs sampling.

An opinionated framework for Bayesian hierarchical modelling of ratios,
rates, and proportions. The core premise is non-negotiable:

\strong{Ratios are not data. They are derived quantities.}

All inference is performed on the latent processes generating the numerator
and the denominator, never on their quotient. Ratios, rates, and proportions
are computed post hoc with full uncertainty propagation.
}
